"The app that turned on Secure Input (PID %d) has quit, but macOS has not turned it off. Third-party input methods, including McBopomofo, cannot be used until then.\n\nPlease log out and log in again." = "The app that turned on Secure Input (PID %d) has quit, but macOS has not turned it off. Third-party input methods, including McBopomofo, cannot be used until then.\n\nPlease log out and log in again.";
"macOS reports that the login window has turned on Secure Input, which usually comes from a password manager or a password field in a browser. Third-party input methods, including McBopomofo, cannot be used while it is on.\n\nPlease try:\n1. Quit the password manager, such as 1Password, completely.\n2. Close the pages or windows waiting for a password.\n3. Lock the screen and unlock it with your password.\n4. Log out and log in again." = "macOS reports that the login window has turned on Secure Input, which usually comes from a password manager or a password field in a browser. Third-party input methods, including McBopomofo, cannot be used while it is on.\n\nPlease try:\n1. Quit the password manager, such as 1Password, completely.\n2. Close the pages or windows waiting for a password.\n3. Lock the screen and unlock it with your password.\n4. Log out and log in again.";
"\"%@\" (PID %d) has turned on Secure Input for more than a minute and a half. Third-party input methods, including McBopomofo, cannot be used while it is on.\n\nIf McBopomofo is gray in the input menu, please try:\n1. Close the pages or windows in the app waiting for a password.\n2. Quit the app completely and open it again.\n3. For a terminal, turn off \"Secure Keyboard Entry\".\n4. Lock the screen and unlock it, or log out and log in again.\n\nThe app name reported by macOS may not be accurate." = "\"%@\" (PID %d) has turned on Secure Input for more than a minute and a half. Third-party input methods, including McBopomofo, cannot be used while it is on.\n\nIf McBopomofo is gray in the input menu, please try:\n1. Close the pages or windows in the app waiting for a password.\n2. Quit the app completely and open it again.\n3. For a terminal, turn off \"Secure Keyboard Entry\".\n4. Lock the screen and unlock it, or log out and log in again.\n\nThe app name reported by macOS may not be accurate.";
